    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R006/argument/@S002/text",
      "value": "For any 0<=sigma<=1 and three arbitrary static mean-zero H^sigma inputs h1,h2,h3, apply E002 with alpha_s=sigma on the same arbitrary interval. The same norm conversion gives ||Cop_I(h1,h2,h3)||_2<=C_sigma |I|^sigma product_j||hj||_(H^sigma). For |I|=0 the integral vanishes. Polynomial approximation and the trilinear bound provide the continuous extension: expand a difference in one slot at a time and use completeness of L2. This proves the static assertion with these arbitrary inputs, which may be renamed f1,f2,f3 in the export."
