    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/graph/inferences/@R002/argument/@S001/text",
      "value": "Fix tau>0 and real alpha,beta. If either phase is zero the definition of eta gives zero. Otherwise put hcov(s)=exp(-i*alpha*s)-M_tau(exp(-i*alpha*s)), with s in [0,tau]. Then eta=tau^(-1)integral hcov(s)exp(-i*beta*s)ds. The identity hcov(s)=tau^(-1)integral_0^tau(exp(-i*alpha*s)-exp(-i*alpha*r))dr and the bound |exp(ix)-exp(iy)|<=|x-y| give |hcov(s)|<=tau*|alpha|, and more precisely |hcov(0)|+|hcov(tau)|<=tau*|alpha|. Also integral_0^tau |hcov'(s)|ds=tau*|alpha|. Taking absolute values gives |eta|<=tau|alpha|. Integrating the beta exponential once gives |eta|<=(|hcov(0)|+|hcov(tau)|+integral|hcov'|)/(tau|beta|)<=2|alpha/beta|. Interchanging phases proves both asserted minima. All integrations are of smooth scalar functions on a compact interval."
    },
